**Task 4.3: Optimize typography for mobile reading** is now complete.

## Summary of Changes

I've implemented comprehensive typography optimizations for mobile reading:

### CSS Optimizations (`app/globals.css`)
- **Mobile font sizes**: 16px base on mobile with responsive scaling
- **Line heights**: 1.75 on mobile, 1.8 for Chinese text
- **Letter spacing**: Optimized for mobile screens
- **Reading width**: 65ch max on desktop, 100% on mobile for optimal comprehension
- **Text selection**: Styled with brand orange accent color
- **Touch-friendly links**: Better spacing for mobile interaction
- **Text size adjust**: Prevents unwanted mobile zoom

### MDX Content Updates (`components/mdx-content.tsx`)
- Headings use `text-balance` for better line breaking
- Paragraphs use `leading-relaxed-mobile` and `reading-width`
- Lists have improved spacing (space-y-2 on mobile)
- Blockquotes have better padding and line height
- Links use `break-words` instead of `break-all` for better flow
- Enhanced inline code and table cell sizes

### Article Page Updates (`app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx`)
- Title has `leading-tight` and `text-balance`
- Metadata text sizes increased for readability
- Summary uses `leading-relaxed-mobile`
- Tag badges have better sizing
- Prose size changed to `prose-base sm:prose-lg`

**Build verified successfully** - All changes are working correctly.
